You do not normally re-send Turnstile on every API request.
Recommended Cloudflare baseline rules
These are baseline examples for an Enterprise Bot Management environment. Tune thresholds after reviewing real traffic in Security Analytics and Bot Analytics.
Rule 1 — Block obvious bots on the API
(http.host eq "api.example.com" and cf.bot_management.score le 10 and not cf.bot_management.verified_bot)
Action: Block
Rule 2 — Managed Challenge suspicious traffic on sensitive routes
(http.host eq "api.example.com" and http.request.uri.path matches "^/api/(auth|token|login|password-reset|upload)" and cf.bot_management.score le 50 and not cf.bot_management.verified_bot)
Action: Managed Challenge
Rule 3 — Rate limit high-risk POST endpoints
Create rate-limiting rules for POST requests to login, token issuance, password reset, and upload routes. Start conservatively, observe traffic, then tighten thresholds based on real usage patterns.
